<%# module_check.js — DOES THE SERVED PAGE ACTUALLY HAVE THESE MODULES?
    A reported DecisionContract undefined in a live browser on 2026-08-14, with
    the script tag above present in the repo since ca034f3 and
    script_load_order.test.js green the whole time. Both were true: the test asks
    what the template says, the browser answers what the server served, and a
    cached compiled template or an unrestarted process breaks that link without
    touching the file the test reads.

    So the page checks itself at runtime and puts a banner up naming anything
    missing. It repairs nothing — the failure was not that a module was absent,
    it was that the panel degraded silently and nothing said so. Loaded LAST so
    every global it asks about has had its chance to define itself. %>
<script src="/js/draft/module_check.js"></script>
